---
/**
 * "We filled these in from your last visit."
 *
 * Restoring a form silently is unsettling — a client who half-remembers
 * starting this cannot tell whether the answers on screen are theirs, ours, or
 * a mistake. So the page says what it did, when the answers are from, and
 * offers the one way out.
 *
 * Blue rather than neutral, which is the one place this page spends a colour on
 * something other than an error: on these pages blue means "where things
 * currently stand", and a restored draft is exactly that. The treatment matches
 * the error summary so the two read as the same kind of object.
 *
 * Two tones, and the client script picks between them by setting `data-tone`. A
 * draft that came back whole is information. One the script had to migrate —
 * which means answers to changed questions were dropped — is a warning, and the
 * band says so in colour as well as in words rather than reporting a loss in
 * the same voice as a restoration. Both come from the semantic variables, so
 * the script never names a colour and a theme can recolour both.
 *
 * role="status" rather than "alert": this is worth announcing when the page
 * settles, but it must not interrupt or take focus the way a failed submission
 * does.
 */
---

<div
	id="questionnaire-restored"
	role="status"
	hidden
	data-tone="info"
	class="q-band q-restore q-tone-info ww-restore"
>
	<div class="ww-restore-row">
		<p class="ww-body ww-muted ww-restore-message" data-restore-message></p>

		{/* A real button, not a link: it changes state rather than going
		    anywhere, and it is the only destructive control on the page — so it
		    confirms before it clears. */}
		<button type="button" class="ww-link ww-restore-action" data-start-fresh>Start fresh</button>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.ww-restore {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
	}

	.ww-restore-row {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: baseline;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
	}

	.ww-restore-message {
		max-width: 58ch;
	}

	.ww-restore-action {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		background: none;
		border: 0;
		padding: 0;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
</style>
